"""v253: the 3D ground, quality and realism only (his photos of Bear Canyon, 11-24 09:38: "Improve quality and realism
only. Do not reinterpret or redesign."). Line maps: sandstone rock with bedding that follows the contours, joints, lichen,
and dark streaks; red soil with stones; dry grass with green patches; a fine relief (normal) map; shading in hollows from
the land's own horizon; a sky-tinted ambient light, a lower and warmer sun from the same side, and soft shadows.
Heights, where rock sits and how far it reaches, the emotion colors at 60 percent, the ways, notes, and labels are unchanged.
Place maps are untouched (Broadview pixel-identical).
Usage: python3 v253_realism.py tools/relief/relief.js gsm-readable.js"""
import sys
R, G = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]
def patch(P, pairs):
    s = open(P).read()
    for a, b in pairs:
        c = s.count(a); assert c == 1, (P, c, a[:90]); s = s.replace(a, b)
    open(P, 'w').write(s)
